  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1021 PM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nRain and storm chances will continue on Saturday before the upper\ntrough goes its own way and allows us to dry back out. High \npressure will build back in after Saturday, so we can look forward\nto low (or no) rain chances from Sunday at least through Thursday\nnight. Storm total QPF values for the next 7 days range from 1/4\"\nto 1/2\" for most of Middle Tennessee, with the bulk of that \nhappening this weekend. Meanwhile, temperatures will warm to or \nabove seasonal norms starting on Sunday, with temperatures on \nMonday and Tuesday likely to warm even more. At this time, it \nappears that heat indices from Sunday through Tuesday will get \nvery close to heat advisory criteria, so it is possible that an \nadvisory will be needed for at least a portion of that period. \nStorm total QPF values for the next 7 days range from 1/4\" to 1/2\"\nfor most of Middle Tennessee.",
